    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0642" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v15/pg609"/>

                <head>147. Transcript of Telephone Conversation Between Secretary of State Kissinger
                    and Soviet Ambassador Dobrynin<anchor n="1" xml:id="d147-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1973-10-24T22:15:00-04:00">October 24, 1973,
                            10:15 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>K. We are assembling our people to consider your letter.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d147-f2"/> I just wanted you to know if any unilateral action is
                    taken before we have had a chance to reply that will be very serious.</p>
                <p>D. Yes, all right.</p>
                <p>K. This is a matter of great concern. Don’t you pressure us. I want to repeat
                    again, don’t pressure us!</p>
                <p>D. All right.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
